# Kernel configuration fragment for a slim PC image: what is particular to
# an x86 machine, on top of configs/slim-common.fragment beside this.
#
# Every symbol below was checked against this kernel's own configuration,
# as in the common fragment.
#
# What is deliberately left alone, because the image would stop working:
#
#  * AHCI, NVMe, and Intel/Realtek/Broadcom ethernet: how it finds a disk
#    and a network on real hardware.
#  * the framebuffer console, i915 and nouveau, which is what an x86
#    machine is likely to need to show anything at all.
#  * everything qemu/kvm needs to boot this image for a quick try: the
#    virtio drivers, KVM guest support, the bochs display qemu defaults
#    to, e1000 and rtl8139, 9p, and the serial console.

# Graphics: keep the drivers an x86 machine is actually likely to have
# and drop the rest. bochs stays with them: it is what qemu's default
# display is, and an image that cannot be booted in a virtual machine
# cannot easily be tried.
# CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_RADEON is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_AST is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_CIRRUS_QEMU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_GMA500 is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_HYPERV is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_MGAG200 is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_QXL is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_UDL is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_VBOXVIDEO is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_VMWGFX is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_XEN_FRONTEND is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_I2C_CH7006 is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_I2C_SIL164 is not set

# Ethernet drivers, by vendor. Intel, Realtek and Broadcom cover the
